      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Tech domain is a strong axis for explaining regional clustering (e.g. biotech vs fintech hubs). Values are well-grounded readings of descriptions (23andMe->healthtech, Addepar->fintech), and silent rows correctly get Unknown/NULL. High NULL count reflects appropriate abstention, not fabrication."
    },
    {
      "name": "industry_vertical",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Vertical gives a genuine grouping axis for clustering analysis. Mostly grounded, though 'enterprise_software' is applied heavily (91) and somewhat by default (e.g. 280 Group, a PM consulting firm, labeled enterprise_software is a stretch), introducing mild over-assertion. Silent rows correctly Unknown."
    },
    {
      "name": "company_stage",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Stage is a plausibly useful trait to correlate with location (e.g. Sand Hill Rd funds). But descriptions rarely state maturity; '23andMe->established' and '280 Group->growth_stage' are confident specifics not supported by the source text. Investor_or_fund labels are well warranted, but many stage assignments appear inferred beyond evidence."
    },
    {
      "name": "target_market",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "B2B/B2C split is a reasonable analytical axis, though heavily skewed toward b2b_enterprise (145) making it near-constant and thus lower leverage. Values are generally sound readings; VC firms and consultancies as b2b_enterprise is defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "delivery_model",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Delivery model adds a business-model axis distinct from tech domain. Values are largely grounded (280 Group->services_consulting, Addepar->saas_cloud). Partially overlaps with hardware_software_orientation but still distinct enough."
    },
    {
      "name": "hardware_software_orientation",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.5,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Grounded and reasonable, but substantially redundant with delivery_model (services_consulting<->services_only, saas_cloud<->primarily_software track closely), reducing its marginal analytical leverage for this query."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
  "source_groundedness": 0.77,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide several genuine axes (tech domain, vertical, delivery model, target market) that support analyzing regional clustering by company traits. Grounding is generally sound with correct abstention on silent rows, but company_stage over-asserts maturity not present in text, and hardware_software_orientation is largely redundant with delivery_model. Overall a useful, mostly well-grounded set with some inferential over-reach."
